* ============================================================================
* MCP4451-103 - quad 8-bit (257-tap) I2C digital potentiometer, 10 kOhm, simple models (2026-09-28)
* Not a Microchip model.  RAB = 10 kOhm and 257 taps are from Microchip's MCP4451 product page (read 2026-09-28).
* The data sheet (DS22267) is a PDF download and was NOT read.  Unverified, assumed from Microchip's usual
* digital-pot convention:
*   RWB = RAB * CODE/256 + RW, so CODE 0 puts the wiper at terminal B and CODE 256 at terminal A;
*   wiper resistance RW = 75 ohm typ;
*   power-on wiper value = mid-scale (CODE 128); the firmware must write the wanted code after power-up.
* On the board each pot has A = GND and B = the 22k/1k divider node, so a HIGHER code gives a LOWER LED current.
* The wiper drives only an op-amp input and 1 nF, so RW does not change the DC result.
* NOT MODELLED: RAB tolerance (it shifts the 22k/1k divider by about 2 % for +/-20 %), temperature,
* terminal capacitances, the I2C interface (the code is a parameter, not written over SCL/SDA).
*
* MCP4451_POT: one potentiometer (units A, B, C of U26 = P0, P1, P2).  Pins A W B.  Parameter CODE (0-256).
* MCP4451_CTRL: the control/supply unit (U26E).  Pins VDD VSS SCL SDA HVC/A0 A1 RESET; high-impedance loads only.
* ============================================================================
.SUBCKT MCP4451_POT A W B PARAMS: CODE=128 RAB=10k RW=75
RB B WI {max(RAB*min(max(CODE,0),256)/256,1m)}
RA WI A {max(RAB*(256-min(max(CODE,0),256))/256,1m)}
RWP WI W {RW}
.ENDS MCP4451_POT

.SUBCKT MCP4451_CTRL VDD VSS SCL SDA HVC_A0 A1 RESET
R1 VDD VSS 1G
R2 SCL VSS 1G
R3 SDA VSS 1G
R4 HVC_A0 VSS 1G
R5 A1 VSS 1G
R6 RESET VSS 1G
.ENDS MCP4451_CTRL
